<h1>Monitoring</h1>
<div class="detail-content">

<p>Prometheus and Grafana form the central monitoring stack for the whole
homelab, running as Docker containers on the NAS. The main Proxmox host,
the two monitored Docker hosts (docker-host-pve and docker-host-nas), the
Synology NAS, and the Raspberry Pi devices feed metrics into this central
instance.</p>

<h2>What's monitored</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Proxmox host metrics</strong>, a PVE exporter reports node-level and per-VM/LXC CPU, memory, and disk metrics into a dedicated Grafana dashboard.</li>
<li><strong>Host metrics on the main machines</strong>, a node exporter runs on the main Proxmox host, both monitored Docker hosts, the NAS, and every Raspberry Pi, feeding basic CPU/RAM/disk/network stats.</li>
<li><strong>Container metrics</strong>, cAdvisor runs on both monitored Docker hosts and the NAS, breaking down resource usage per container.</li>
<li><strong>Network hardware via SNMP</strong>, an SNMP exporter polls the FRITZ!Box, the Zyxel switches, the OpenWrt router, and a network-attached printer for uptime, throughput, toner level, page count and status.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Dashboards</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Dashboard</th><th>Focus</th></tr>
<tr><td>Proxmox monitoring (extended)</td><td>Node-level and per-guest VM/LXC metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Docker container monitoring</td><td>Per-container CPU/memory/network/disk</td></tr>
<tr><td>Network infrastructure</td><td>FRITZ!Box, Zyxel switches and OpenWrt via SNMP</td></tr>
<tr><td>Network printer</td><td>Toner level, page count, online/offline status via SNMP</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>How it's deployed</h2>
<p>Prometheus runs as a Docker container on the Synology NAS with a
bind-mounted data directory for persistence. Grafana is deployed as a
sibling container, connected to Prometheus as its primary datasource.
Both containers are defined in a single Docker Compose file and managed
via Portainer. The Prometheus configuration file defines scrape targets,
scrape intervals (15 seconds for hosts, 60 seconds for network devices),
and retention policies.</p>

<h2>Alerting</h2>
<p>There is no central Alertmanager channel. Uptime Kuma watches service
reachability, and Healthchecks covers scheduled jobs with a dead-man's-switch
pattern: if a backup, sync or other job does not report in, the missed check
raises the alert. More sophisticated Prometheus alerting rules (disk space
prediction, temperature thresholds) are not configured yet.</p>

<h2>Visitor analytics</h2>
<p>Metrics are not the only signal. <a href="/infra/web-analytics/">Web Log Analytics</a> reads Apache and nginx access logs and reports weekly visitors, bots, scanners and per-vhost traffic. It is intentionally separate from Prometheus, which tracks system health rather than audience behavior.</p>

<h2>Open items</h2>
<ul>
<li>Prometheus alerting rules are not configured for most services.</li>
<li>The secondary Proxmox host (pve2) is always on for the Xubuntu dev VM, but it is not monitored yet.</li>
<li>Retention policy for Prometheus data hasn't been tuned.</li>
</ul>

